+# Federation Master Organization Plan — Clean Parity, Upstream Sync & Zero-Orphan Architecture
+
+**Work Order:** Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open#471 (P1-high, documentation)
+**Agent:** zai-autonomous-contributor (Z.ai Code, zero-credential bridge lane)
+**Scope:** new files only — this plan plus the single-command parity checker it ships
+**Aligned with:** AUTONOMOUS_TRANSIT_PIPELINE rules 1-15 (claim-and-branch pipeline) and the gateway specification rules 18-22
+**Tooling shipped:** docs/federation_parity_check.py (stdlib-only, offline self-test 4/4 PASS)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Purpose
+
+Fourteen repositories ship one product. This plan makes their relationship
+mechanical instead of tribal: every contract file has exactly one source of
+truth, every satellite receives changes without a human copy step, and the
+whole federation's sync health is answerable with one command.
+
+## 2. Federation Directory (current state, verbatim from WO #471)
+
+| # | Repository | Status | Role | Next action |
+|---|------------|--------|------|-------------|
+| 1 | supremeai-open | Live | Public ingress, bridge proxy | Keep board clean, prune transits |
+| 2 | supremeai | Live | Core monolith anchor | Gates + constitutional engine |
+| 3 | supremeai-mcp-control-plane | Live | MCP tower on Render | Deploy 5-core tool diet, mcp + sse transports |
+| 4 | supremeai-api | Pending | Unified provider gateway | Gateway shield, vault keys, failover (WO #469) |
+| 5 | supremeai-studio | Clean | Web UI dashboard | CORS fixed, live |
+| 6 | supremeai-browser | Ready | Stealth automation sandbox | High-fidelity runtime (WO #461) |
+| 7 | supremeai-sdk | Clean | Client SDK packages | Python + TS packaging landed |
+| 8 | supremeai-infrastructure | Clean | Render and Terraform ops | Zero-secret blueprint landed |
+| 9 | supremeai-agents | Pending | Stateless agent lifecycle | Loop dispatcher harness sync |
+| 10 | supremeai-skills | Backlog | Skills marketplace | Capability registry |
+| 11 | supremeai-command | Clean | Telegram admin control | Remote trigger and webhook dispatch |
+| 12 | supremeai-vscode | Clean | IDE extension | Developer agent hooks |
+| 13 | supremeai-archive | Clean | Append-only memory | Worklogs and ADRs |
+| 14 | supremeai-core | Private | Proprietary moat | Decision intelligence |
+
+## 3. Milestone 1 — Mirror Parity Automation
+
+### 3.1 Parity classes
+
+- **BYTE-IDENTICAL** — landed contracts that must be sha256-equal everywhere:
+  docs/CONSUMERS.md, api-schemas/gateway.openapi.yaml, api-schemas/heartbeat.schema.json
+  (the manifest lives in the checker and grows only by PR).
+- **CURATED** — per-repo surfaces that are intentionally different
+  (READMEs, dashboards, extension manifests). Never parity-checked; drift here is design, not defect.
+
+### 3.2 Mechanism
+
+The checker fetches each manifest path from the open baseline at raw
+githubusercontent under the main branch, hashes it, fetches the same path
+from every declaring satellite, and compares. Four verdicts, fail-loud:
+
+- PARITY — all copies byte-identical
+- DRIFT — same path, different bytes (gate failure)
+- MISSING — a satellite declares the contract but lacks the file (gate failure)
+- UNREACHABLE — private plane or network fault (skip with warning, never silent)
+
+### 3.3 Gate integration
+
+CI-optional by design: the tool is deterministic and side-effect free, so the
+pipeline can call it in check mode after landing and fail the gate on DRIFT or
+MISSING. Exit codes 0/1/2/3 are documented in the module docstring. Operator
+can run the same command locally — one vocabulary, two consumers.
+
+## 4. Milestone 2 — Zero-Duplicate Rule
+
+The landing workflow already streams public merges to satellites by reference
+(patch branch fetched by exact head SHA, immutable). This plan codifies the
+operating rules that keep it duplicate-free:
+
+1. One dispatcher — never add a second trigger channel to the landing workflow.
+2. No manual satellite PRs for content that routes through landing.yml;
+   duplication is created exactly there, so it is banned exactly there.
+3. Satellite-bound file placement follows the routing table (direct-children
+   matching, per lesson L6): api and gateway prefixes to the API repo,
+   browser and sandbox prefixes to the browser repo, docs and scripts-agents
+   prefixes to the anchor.
+4. Bridge orders exist only for landed patches — a WO is a record, not a request.
+
+## 5. Milestone 3 — Federation Health Dashboard
+
+Single command, no install:
+
+```
+python3 docs/federation_parity_check.py --report
+```
+
+Emits the per-contract verdict table plus a final PASS/FAIL gate line.
+ECOSYSTEM_MAP.md stays the human-readable dashboard (operator-curated);
+this tool is its data source, so map edits can cite checker output instead
+of memory. Recommended cadence: after every landing batch, and before any
+satellite release cut.
+
+## 6. Per-Repo Next Actions (priority order)
+
+1. supremeai-api — implement WO #469 (shield, vault-only keys, SSOT key, quota plane)
+2. supremeai-browser — implement WO #461 (high-fidelity client runtime)
+3. supremeai-agents — sync continuous loop dispatcher harness with the anchor loop
+4. supremeai-skills — seed capability registry from the skills marketplace spec
+5. Anchor — adopt the parity gate into post-landing CI (one-line call)
+
+## 7. Rollout and Rollback
+
+- Rollout: land this plan plus the checker; run report once to snapshot the
+  current parity baseline; wire the check call into post-landing CI.
+- Rollback: docs-only delivery — deleting the two files restores the prior
+  state with zero runtime exposure. No workflow, schema, or service file is touched.
+
+## 8. Verification Evidence
+
+- Checker compile: py_compile PASS
+- Checker offline self-test: 4/4 scenario groups PASS (parity, drift, missing, unreachable)
+- Routing conformance: both files match the anchor lane path allowlist (docs/*)
+- New-files-only doctrine: no existing file modified
+- Secret scan: no credential material; manifest contains repo names and public paths only
+
